{"name":"Tender Limerence","hex":"#e0d4e0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sensitive or painful to the touch.","Easily bruised or injured; not firm or hard; delicate."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Care, kind concern, regard.","The inner flight muscle (pectoralis minor) of poultry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tender"},{"term":"limerence","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An involuntary romantic infatuation with another person, especially combined with an overwhelming, obsessive need to have one's feelings reciprocated. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limerence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limerence","blocks":[{"text":"Limerence is the mental state of being madly in love or intensely infatuated when reciprocation of the feeling is uncertain. This state is characterized by intrusive thoughts and idealization of the loved one, typically with a desire for reciprocation to form a relationship. This is accompanied by feelings of ecstasy or despair, depending on whether one's feelings seem to be reciprocated or not."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Antonio_Canova_-_Psych%C3%A9_ranim%C3%A9e_par_le_baiser_de_l%27Amour%2C_Marbre%2C_1793.jpg/330px-Antonio_Canova_-_Psych%C3%A9_ranim%C3%A9e_par_le_baiser_de_l%27Amour%2C_Marbre%2C_1793.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limerence"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Henry_Holiday_-_Dante_and_Beatrice_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Henry_Holiday_-_Dante_and_Beatrice_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Henry_Holiday_-_Dante_and_Beatrice_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Henry_Holiday_-_Dante_and_Beatrice_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Henry_Holiday_-_Dante_and_Beatrice_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Henry_Holiday_-_Dante_and_Beatrice_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dante and Beatrice, by Henry Holiday, depicts Beatrice refusing to speak to Dante, an event which according to Dante left him so overcome with sorrow that he bitterly cried himself to sleep, \"like a little child [...] after it has been beaten\".[76][77]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHenry_Holiday_-_Dante_and_Beatrice_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rogelio_de_Egusquiza_-_Tristan_and_Isolt_%28Death%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Rogelio_de_Egusquiza_-_Tristan_and_Isolt_%28Death%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rogelio_de_Egusquiza_-_Tristan_and_Isolt_%28Death%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-Rogelio_de_Egusquiza_-_Tristan_and_Isolt_%28Death%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Rogelio_de_Egusquiza_-_Tristan_and_Isolt_%28Death%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Rogelio_de_Egusquiza_-_Tristan_and_Isolt_%28Death%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tristan and Isolde (Death), by Rogelio de Egusquiza. In this myth, the two drink a love potion by mistake, when Iseult is due to be married to Tristan's uncle, a king. In one version of the story, Tristan dies of a broken heart after a signal sent by Iseult is miscommunicated to him as a rejection.[99] In another version, Tristan is mortally wounded but Iseult cannot save him and gives up her spirit. The story is said to be the quintessential courtly romance.[100]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARogelio_de_Egusquiza_-_Tristan_and_Isolt_(Death)_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Frederick_Goodall_RA_-_Passionate_encounter.jpg/330px-Frederick_Goodall_RA_-_Passionate_encounter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Frederick_Goodall_RA_-_Passionate_encounter.jpg/330px-Frederick_Goodall_RA_-_Passionate_encounter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrederick_Goodall_RA_-_Passionate_encounter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/La_Promenade%2C_by_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir.jpg/500px-La_Promenade%2C_by_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/La_Promenade%2C_by_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir.jpg/1280px-La_Promenade%2C_by_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/La_Promenade%2C_by_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir.jpg/500px-La_Promenade%2C_by_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALa_Promenade%2C_by_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Peacock_Plumage.jpg/500px-Peacock_Plumage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Peacock_Plumage.jpg/1280px-Peacock_Plumage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"h